IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cla2-common`

-- Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) -- baseline-2026-11: Part 2 Division 5, provisional and subsequent damages for dust
-- diseases (ss 15AA-15AO, inserted by No. 32 of 2024, in operation from 1 December 2024).
--
-- SEAT. The person who has a dust disease (from inhaling asbestos or silica) and sues, or has sued, for personal injury
-- damages: the plaintiff. Every question is asked as that person would ask it.
--
-- The Division lets a plaintiff take damages now for the disease they have (provisional damages) and come back later for a
-- further dust disease named at the start (subsequent damages), instead of one final award. "the Court" is the Supreme
-- Court (s 15AA).
--
-- Out: s 15AD (the court "must not assume" the later disease; no input changes it, finding 9), s 15AH(3)-(7) (the court's
-- suppression and non-publication orders), s 15AI (evidence), s 15AN (costs: the court "must have regard to" earlier costs;
-- no figure follows). s 15AH(2) and s 15AK are "must consider"/"must take into account" duties of the court; s 15AK is
-- encoded as the total the court must take into account, not as a deduction.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Part 2 Division 5 -- dust diseases`

§§ `s 15AB -- is my condition a dust disease`

DECLARE `Where the condition is` IS ONE OF
    `the lungs`
    `the pleura`
    `the peritoneum`
    `elsewhere in the body`

-- s 15AB Table.
DECLARE `The listed disease` IS ONE OF
    `asbestosis`
    `asbestos-induced carcinoma`
    `asbestos-related pleural disease`
    `lung cancer`
    `mesothelioma`
    `pneumoconiosis or silicosis`
    `silicotuberculosis`
    `none of the listed diseases`

-- s 15AB: "A dust disease means a pathological condition that is either or both of the following -- (a) a pathological
-- condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum that has resulted from the inhalation of asbestos or silica; (b) a pathological
-- condition specified in the Table (whether or not of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum) that has resulted from the inhalation
-- of asbestos or silica." A "means" definition: JUST FALSE when it fails. That the condition is "pathological" is taken as
-- given (a diagnosed condition).
@export Is my condition a dust disease under the Civil Liability Act (s 15AB)?
GIVEN
    `where it is` IS A `Where the condition is` @desc Where in your body is the condition: the lungs, the pleura (the lining of the lungs), the peritoneum (the lining of the abdomen), or elsewhere?
    `which listed disease` IS A `The listed disease` @desc Which of these is your diagnosis, if any: asbestosis, asbestos-induced carcinoma, asbestos-related pleural disease, lung cancer, mesothelioma, pneumoconiosis or silicosis, silicotuberculosis?
    `it came from inhaling asbestos or silica` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the condition result from breathing in asbestos or silica (for example, dust from engineered stone)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my condition a dust disease` IS
    IF `it is a dust disease` `where it is` `which listed disease` `it came from inhaling asbestos or silica`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `where it is` IS A `Where the condition is`, `which listed disease` IS A `The listed disease`, `from dust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a dust disease` IF
        `from dust`
    AND (   (NOT (`where it is` EQUALS `elsewhere in the body`))
         OR (NOT (`which listed disease` EQUALS `none of the listed diseases`)))

§§ `ss 15AC, 15AO, 3A -- can I be awarded provisional damages`

-- s 15AC(1): "In an action (an initial action) in respect of a dust disease suffered by a plaintiff for which personal injury
-- damages are claimed, the Court may award damages (provisional damages) on a provisional basis for that dust disease."
-- (2): "provisional damages can only be awarded if the initial action is commenced in the Court by an indorsed writ or a
-- writ indorsed with a statement of claim ... that -- (a) nominates provisional damages as the remedy required; and (b)
-- specifies another dust disease (a subsequent dust disease) or more than 1 subsequent dust disease that the plaintiff may
-- develop, wholly or partly as a result of the act or omission giving rise to the cause of action."
-- s 15AO(2): an action "commenced before proclamation day" (1 December 2024) may be amended to nominate provisional damages
-- and specify the subsequent dust diseases; (3): not if, before that day, "(a) the hearing of the action has commenced; or (b)
-- damages have been awarded or a settlement reached in the action"; (4): an amended claim in another court is transferred
-- to the Supreme Court. The encoder reads an amendment under s 15AO(2) as meeting s 15AC(2) for such an action (fork F3).
-- s 3A: Division 5 is off for items 1, 2, 4 and 5 (see cla2-common.l4): NOTHING (the Division does not reach the claim).
-- The award is the court's discretion ("may"): JUST TRUE means it can be awarded, not that it will be.
-- "can only be awarded if": JUST FALSE when s 15AC(2) is not met. Not a dust disease: s 15AC is silent (NOTHING).
@export Can the Supreme Court award me provisional damages for my dust disease, so that I can claim again if I develop another (ss 15AC, 15AO, 3A)?
GIVEN
    `where it is` IS A `Where the condition is` @desc Where in your body is the condition: the lungs, the pleura (the lining of the lungs), the peritoneum (the lining of the abdomen), or elsewhere?
    `which listed disease` IS A `The listed disease` @desc Which of these is your diagnosis, if any: asbestosis, asbestos-induced carcinoma, asbestos-related pleural disease, lung cancer, mesothelioma, pneumoconiosis or silicosis, silicotuberculosis?
    `it came from inhaling asbestos or silica` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the condition result from breathing in asbestos or silica (for example, dust from engineered stone)?
    `the class of my damages` IS A `The class of my damages under s 3A` @desc Apart from being a dust claim (item 6), does your claim also fall in another class of the s 3A Table? Choose item 6 if not.
    `I claim personal injury damages for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming damages for the disease from the person whose fault caused it (not a superannuation or insurance benefit)?
    `the date my action was commenced` IS A DATE @desc The date your action for the disease was started in court
    `it was commenced in the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your action started in the Supreme Court of Western Australia?
    `my writ nominates provisional damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your writ (or, for an action started before 1 December 2024, your claim as amended) nominate provisional damages as the remedy you seek?
    `how many later dust diseases my writ specifies` IS A NUMBER @desc How many other dust diseases that you may develop from the same exposure does your writ (or amended claim) specify?
    `the hearing began before 1 December 2024` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an action started before 1 December 2024: had the hearing of the action begun before that day?
    `damages or a settlement before 1 December 2024` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an action started before 1 December 2024: had damages been awarded, or a settlement been reached, in the action before that day?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be awarded provisional damages` IS
    IF (NOT (`it is a dust disease` `where it is` `which listed disease` `it came from inhaling asbestos or silica`))
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `Division 5 is taken away by s 3A` `the class of my damages`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF (NOT `I claim personal injury damages for it`)
              THEN NOTHING
              ELSE IF `the writ meets s 15AC(2)`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the writ names the remedy and a later disease` MEANS
                `my writ nominates provisional damages`
            AND `how many later dust diseases my writ specifies` AT LEAST 1
        `the writ meets s 15AC(2)` MEANS
            IF `is before proclamation day` `the date my action was commenced`
            THEN     `the writ names the remedy and a later disease`
                 AND (NOT `the hearing began before 1 December 2024`)
                 AND (NOT `damages or a settlement before 1 December 2024`)
            ELSE     `the writ names the remedy and a later disease`
                 AND `it was commenced in the Supreme Court`

§§ `ss 15AG, 15AJ -- can I sue again for a later dust disease`

DECLARE `How my initial action ended` IS ONE OF
    `it was not settled in whole by a settlement agreement`
    `settled in whole; the agreement says I am not barred from a subsequent action for this disease`
    `settled in whole; the agreement bars a subsequent action for some other disease but not this one`
    `settled in whole; the agreement says I am barred from a subsequent action for this disease`

-- s 15AG(1): "In an action (a subsequent action) in respect of a subsequent dust disease for which personal injury damages are
-- claimed, the Court may award damages (subsequent damages)". (2): it "must be commenced in the Court". (3): it "must be in
-- respect of a subsequent dust disease specified in the ... writ ... that commenced the initial action". (5): "a plaintiff
-- cannot commence a subsequent action in relation to a subsequent dust disease that has already been the subject of a
-- subsequent action". (6): "A plaintiff is barred from commencing a subsequent action if -- (a) the initial action was
-- disposed of in whole by a settlement agreement that specifies that the plaintiff is barred from commencing a subsequent
-- action; or (b) any other subsequent action was disposed of in whole by a settlement agreement that specifies that the
-- plaintiff is barred from commencing another subsequent action." s 15AJ: "Only 1 award of subsequent damages can be made
-- for each subsequent dust disease".
-- s 15AE(c) has the agreement say "whether or not the plaintiff is barred ... in relation to a subsequent dust disease", one
-- disease at a time; the encoder reads s 15AG(6)(a) the same way, so a bar on another disease leaves this one open (fork
-- F4). For a pre-2024 action the writ includes the claim as amended under s 15AO(2).
-- "must", "cannot", "is barred": JUST FALSE when they bite. s 3A as for provisional damages: NOTHING.
@export Can I bring a further action in the Supreme Court for a later dust disease named in my first action (ss 15AG, 15AJ)?
GIVEN
    `the class of my damages` IS A `The class of my damages under s 3A` @desc Apart from being a dust claim (item 6), does your claim also fall in another class of the s 3A Table? Choose item 6 if not.
    `the disease was named in my first writ` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was this disease specified, as a dust disease you might develop, in the writ (or amended claim) that started your first action?
    `it has already been the subject of a further action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already brought a further (subsequent) action for this same disease?
    `how my initial action ended` IS A `How my initial action ended` @desc Was your first action settled in whole by a settlement agreement, and if so what does the agreement say about further actions for this disease?
    `another further action was settled with a bar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was any other further action of yours settled in whole by an agreement saying you are barred from bringing another further action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I bring a subsequent action for a later dust disease` IS
    IF `Division 5 is taken away by s 3A` `the class of my damages`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF     `the disease was named in my first writ`
            AND (NOT `it has already been the subject of a further action`)
            AND (NOT (`how my initial action ended` EQUALS `settled in whole; the agreement says I am barred from a subsequent action for this disease`))
            AND (NOT `another further action was settled with a bar`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 15AE, 15AL -- what a settlement agreement must say`

-- s 15AE (initial action) and s 15AL (subsequent action): an agreement settling the action "must specify the following --
-- (a) any [other] subsequent dust disease that the plaintiff claims they may develop ...; (b) whether or not the defendant
-- admits liability for -- (i) the [subsequent] dust disease; and (ii) if a[nother] subsequent dust disease is specified in
-- accordance with paragraph (a) -- [that] subsequent dust disease; (c) whether or not the plaintiff is barred from commencing
-- [another] subsequent action in relation to a subsequent dust disease specified in accordance with paragraph (a)."
-- The encoder reads (c) as needed only when (a) specifies a disease (fork F6). The Act says nothing of an agreement that
-- leaves an item out; JUST FALSE means only that it does not say what s 15AE or s 15AL requires.
@export Does my settlement agreement for a dust disease action say everything the Act requires it to (ss 15AE, 15AL)?
GIVEN
    `it names every later dust disease I claim I may develop` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement list every further dust disease you claim you may develop from the same exposure (or say there is none)?
    `how many later dust diseases it names` IS A NUMBER @desc How many further dust diseases does the agreement list?
    `it says whether liability is admitted for the disease settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say whether or not the defendant admits liability for the disease the action is about?
    `it says whether liability is admitted for each later disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say, for each further disease it lists, whether or not the defendant admits liability for it?
    `it says whether I am barred from suing again` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say whether or not you are barred from a further action for the diseases it lists?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my settlement agreement say what the Act requires` IS
    IF     `it names every later dust disease I claim I may develop`
       AND `it says whether liability is admitted for the disease settled`
       AND (    `how many later dust diseases it names` EQUALS 0
            OR (    `it says whether liability is admitted for each later disease`
                AND `it says whether I am barred from suing again`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 15AF, 15AM -- what happens to my action when it settles`

DECLARE `What happens to the settled action` IS ONE OF
    `it must be discontinued, which keeps a further action open`
    `it may be dismissed`
    `the Act does not say`

-- s 15AF(1): an initial action "disposed of in whole by a settlement agreement that specifies that the plaintiff is not barred
-- from commencing a subsequent action in relation to at least 1 subsequent dust disease specified in the settlement agreement
-- ... must be discontinued". (2): one settled by an agreement that "specifies that the plaintiff is barred from commencing a
-- subsequent action in relation to all subsequent dust diseases identified in the ... writ ... may be dismissed".
-- s 15AM(1): a subsequent action settled by an agreement that specifies the plaintiff "is not barred from commencing another
-- subsequent action ... must be discontinued"; (2): one that specifies the plaintiff "is barred ... may be dismissed".
-- The gap: an agreement that says neither -- for an initial action, one that bars some of the writ's diseases but leaves none
-- it lists open (for example, it lists none) -- falls under neither subsection: `the Act does not say` (finding 7). The two
-- sections have the same shape, so one question serves both.
@export What happens to my dust disease action when it is settled in whole: must it be discontinued, or may it be dismissed (ss 15AF, 15AM)?
GIVEN
    `it leaves me free to sue for at least one listed disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the settlement agreement say you are not barred from a further action for at least one further dust disease it lists?
    `it bars me for every disease in my writ` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the settlement agreement say you are barred from a further action for every further dust disease named in your writ (for a further action: barred from any further action)?
GIVETH A `What happens to the settled action`
DECIDE `What happens to my settled dust disease action` IS
    IF `it leaves me free to sue for at least one listed disease`
    THEN `it must be discontinued, which keeps a further action open`
    ELSE IF `it bars me for every disease in my writ`
         THEN `it may be dismissed`
         ELSE `the Act does not say`

§§ `s 15AK -- what earlier amounts count against my subsequent damages`

-- s 15AK: "In determining the amount of subsequent damages to award, the Court must take into account any amount -- (a)
-- awarded to the plaintiff -- (i) in the initial action by way of provisional damages; and (ii) in any other subsequent action
-- by way of subsequent damages; and (b) received by the plaintiff in settlement of -- (i) the initial action; or (ii) any
-- other subsequent action." "Take into account" is not "deduct": the answer is the total the court must weigh, not the
-- amount to be taken off (finding 8).
@export What earlier amounts must the Supreme Court take into account when it sets my damages for a later dust disease (s 15AK)?
GIVEN
    `my provisional damages` IS A NUMBER @desc Provisional damages awarded to you in your first action, in dollars (0 if none)
    `my earlier subsequent damages` IS A NUMBER @desc Damages awarded to you in your other further actions, in dollars (0 if none)
    `what I received in settlements` IS A NUMBER @desc What you received in settlement of your first action or of any other further action, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What earlier amounts count against my subsequent damages` IS
    `my provisional damages` PLUS `my earlier subsequent damages` PLUS `what I received in settlements`
